      term: 'Dynamic Components & KeepAlive',
      importance: 3,
      whyAsked: 'Tab UIs are universal; KeepAlive tests whether you know component state dies on unmount and how caching changes the lifecycle.',
      explanation: '<component :is="comp"> renders a component chosen at runtime; switching unmounts the old one (state lost). Wrapping in <KeepAlive> caches deactivated instances instead of destroying them — state and DOM survive; onActivated/onDeactivated fire instead of mount/unmount cycles. include/exclude filter by component name, max evicts LRU.',
