        'Cut reactivity cost: hold the dataset in a shallowRef and replace the array wholesale on data refresh (triggerRef after batch in-place edits). Deep-proxying 50k nested objects costs memory and every property read goes through a trap.',
        'Make filtering cheap: computed over the raw array with a debounced search ref; if filtering itself takes >50ms, move it to a Web Worker or server-side pagination — 50k rows in the client is often the real design smell.',
        'Row hygiene: stable :key="row.id", v-memo="[row.selected]" on rows if cell content is expensive, event delegation via a single handler on the tbody instead of per-cell listeners.',
